<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1997 crude oil refining seen 170-180 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russian 1997 crude oil refining seen 170-180 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will refine 170-180 million tonnes of crude oil this year, compared with 176 million tonnes in 1996, Fuel and Energy Minister Pyotr Rodionov told an energy conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Russia is struggling to ensure adequate crude oil supplies to its refineries against strong exports to world markets.</p>
<p>Rodionov submitted his resignation last week.</p>
<p>-- Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
